            <ArticleTitle>Update on neuropathic pain treatment: ion channel blockers and gabapentinoids.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>359</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11916-013-0359-2</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neuropathic pain is a debilitating chronic pain condition, which remains difficult to treat. The current mainstays of treatment include physical therapy, interventional procedures and medications. Among medications, ion channel blockers and gabapentinoids are the 2 classes of drugs commonly used to treat neuropathic pain. It has been suggested that these medications may be useful to treat a variety of neuropathic pain conditions. This article provides several updates on the utility of both ion channel blockers and gabapentinoids for the treatment of neuropathic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
